  "slug": "phenotype-biomedical-corpus-b5a5",
  "summary": "Agentic LLM systems now drive robotic culture, molecular dynamics and systems-biology workflows, making auditability a design requirement.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is LLM agents taking on planning and execution of biological workflows, paired with mechanisms that check their outputs. BioMARS 2.0 links literature-grounded protocol generation to feedback-driven culture optimization in a human-in-the-loop robotic system. MDClaw is an auditable harness for AI-agent-run biomolecular dynamics simulations, using validating tools and a DAG to check stages and record provenance. Octomod is an LLM multi-agent workflow built on AMICI, pyPESTO, SBML and PEtab for mechanistic model construction, parameter estimation and hypothesis testing. The review AI for Biologists addresses the knowledge boundary of biological foundation models and agentic systems, defined by data, architecture, training and evaluation. What is new is the extension of agentic control to physical culture and to standardized modelling pipelines, with verification built in. Because all four items are preprints, cross-system comparison of performance remains limited.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
